.TH LOCALPASSKEY-BRIDGE 1 "October 2026" "localpasskey 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
localpasskey-bridge \- native messaging host that lets Chrome and Chromium use LocalPasskey as this device's passkey authenticator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/lib/localpasskey/localpasskey-bridge
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B localpasskey-bridge
is not run by hand. The LocalPasskey browser extension for Google Chrome and
Chromium takes over WebAuthn with the
.B chrome.webAuthenticationProxy
API, and the browser starts the bridge, as you, once for every passkey
request. It reads one native message from standard input (a 4-byte length
followed by JSON), answers on standard output and exits. Closing standard
input cancels a request in progress.
.PP
A create or sign-in request runs on the LocalPasskey virtual security key of
.BR localpasskeyd (8),
found by the USB IDs and product name in
.IR /etc/localpasskey/localpasskeyd.conf .
Other security keys are never used. The usual confirmation dialog appears,
naming the browser that started the bridge (a hint only: any program
running as you can make the dialog show another name). Requests that ask for
a passkey on this device (\fBauthenticatorAttachment: "platform"\fR) are answered too,
which is the reason for the bridge: without it Chrome refuses them on Linux.
.PP
The website's origin is taken from the browser, which checked it against the
site's rp ID, related origins included. The bridge refuses origins that are
not https (other than http://localhost) and requests from cross-origin
iframes. Errors reach the page as a generic
.BR NotAllowedError ,
.B InvalidStateError
(this computer already has one of the passkeys the site listed) or
.B NotSupportedError
(no supported algorithm); they never carry request data.
.SH SETUP
Open
.BR chrome://extensions ,
switch on Developer mode, click Load unpacked and choose
.IR /usr/share/localpasskey/chromium-extension .
Passkey autofill, other security keys, phones and passkeys saved in the
browser are not offered while the extension is on; see the README for all
limitations.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOCALPASSKEY_BRIDGE_DEBUG
If set, log why a request failed (the exception type only) to standard error,
which the browser writes to its own log.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/opt/chrome/native-messaging-hosts/org.localpasskey.bridge.json
.TQ
.I /etc/chromium/native-messaging-hosts/org.localpasskey.bridge.json
Register the bridge with Google Chrome and Chromium, for the LocalPasskey
extension's ID only.
.TP
.I /usr/share/localpasskey/chromium-extension/
The extension.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR localpasskey (1),
.BR localpasskeyd (8)
